From: Predidit <34627277+Predidit@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] network: restore the legacy TLS verification default

Keep mpv and libmpv compatible with this project's previous builds, which
disabled certificate verification by default. Explicit tls-verify=yes
continues to work. This deliberately trades HTTPS authentication for
backwards compatibility; document that in the bundled manual as well.

diff --git a/stream/network.c b/stream/network.c
--- a/stream/network.c
+++ b/stream/network.c
@@ -51,9 +51,7 @@ const struct m_sub_options mp_network_conf = {
     .defaults = &(const struct mp_network_opts){
         .useragent = "libmpv",
         .timeout = 60,
-#if HAVE_LIBCURL || LIBAVFORMAT_VERSION_MAJOR >= 63
-        .tls_verify = true,
-#endif
+        .tls_verify = false,
     },
 };

diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -5742,13 +5742,13 @@ Network
 ``--tls-verify=<yes|no>``
     Verify peer certificates when using TLS (e.g. with ``https://...``)
-    (default: yes*). Disabling this option allows man-in-the-middle attacks
-    to silently substitute the content of an HTTPS stream and is only
+    (default in this build: no). Disabling this option allows man-in-the-middle
+    attacks to silently substitute the content of an HTTPS stream and is only
     recommended as a per-stream override when verification fails for a
     known-good reason (e.g. an outdated CA bundle, a corporate proxy, a
     development server with a self-signed certificate).

-    This is disabled by default, if mpv is built without libcurl and
-    libavformat is older than 63.0.100.
+    This build disables verification by default for backwards compatibility.
+    Use ``--tls-verify=yes`` with a trusted ``--tls-ca-file`` to enable it.

 ``--tls-cert-file``
     A file containing a certificate to use in the handshake with the
